"BadRequestError: no fulcrum entry at ".fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F999-absent.md"

a relative --why is checked two ways, and neither resolved:
   route-relative     = <tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F999-absent.md
   repo-root-relative = <tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F999-absent.md

a dispute cites an argument the council will read, so the entry must exist first.
write it there, then re-run this command:
  <tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F00N-<slug>.md

and pass either the ROUTE-relative path (canonical), or the repo-root-relative one:
  --why .fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F00N-<slug>.md
  --why <tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F00N-<slug>.md

{
  "why": ".fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F999-absent.md",
  "route": "<tempDir>",
  "asRouteRelative": "<tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F999-absent.md",
  "asRepoRootRelative": "<tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F999-absent.md"
}"
`;
